{"name":"Snowdrift Glow","hex":"#d6e5f0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snowdrift","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bank of snow accumulated by the wind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowdrift"},{"term":"glow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To emit heat and light without a flame.","To emit heat and light without a flame."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of heat and light being emitted by a hot object.","A state of heat being emitted by a person or an animal's body."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snowdrift","blocks":[{"text":"A snowdrift is a deposit of snow sculpted by wind into a mound during a snowstorm. Snowdrifts resemble sand dunes and are formed in a similar manner, namely, by wind moving light snow and depositing it when the wind has virtually stopped, usually against a stationary object. Snow normally crests and slopes off toward the surface on the windward side of a large object. On the leeward side, areas near the object are a bit lower than surrounding areas but are generally flatter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/2024-01-21_07_06_48_Snow_drift_along_Burlington_County_Routes_630_and_637_%28Irick_Road%29_near_Woodlane_Road_in_Westampton_Township%2C_Burlington_County%2C_New_Jersey.jpg/330px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowdrift","wikidata":"Q611668"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Long_Mynd_snowdrift.jpeg/250px-Long_Mynd_snowdrift.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Long_Mynd_snowdrift.jpeg/500px-Long_Mynd_snowdrift.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum